{"by":"Hojung Lee","img":"https://theyappie.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/54534383375_d06ce8c383_o-1024x683.jpg","body":"<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This story first appeared in Power Shift, </em>The Yappie<em>'s weekly newsletter on national AAPI power, politics, and influence. <a href=\"https://newsletters.theyappie.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Subscribe for free here.</strong></a></em></p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator alignwide has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The U.S. deported 483,200 people</strong> in fiscal year 2026, surpassing the highest annual figure in the agency’s reported history (set last year), <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ice-deportations-arrests-hit-record-high/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">according to internal figures</a> obtained by <em>CBS News</em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The record comes shortly</strong> after President <strong>Donald Trump</strong> acknowledged that his crackdown on immigration may have been “<a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/10-takeaways-from-trump-60-minutes-interview/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">too tough</a>” and contributed to the <a href=\"https://theyappie.com/what-the-data-tells-us-about-aapi-voters-in-last-weeks-elections/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">midterms blue tsunami</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cbs-news-exit-polls-2026-midterms-democrats/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>CBS News</em></a> <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cbs-news-exit-polls-2026-midterms-democrats/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">exit polling data</a> found that 58% of voters believe the current administration’s immigration enforcement has gone overboard.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Despite this statement,</strong> Trump <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/president-trump-names-stephen-miller-as-33rd-white-house-chief-of-staff/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">has appointed</a> immigration hardliner <strong>Stephen Miller</strong> to replace White House chief of staff <strong>Susie Wiles</strong>.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Miller is the mastermind behind many of the Trump administration’s <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ice-deportations-arrests-hit-record-high/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">most restrictive immigration policies</a> and has reportedly told leadership there are <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/immigration/ice-isnt-slowing-voters-midterms-message-sources-say-rcna607821?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">no plans to slow down</a>, per <em>NBC News</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Our take: </strong>As <em><a href=\"https://theyappie.com/the-hidden-numbers-in-trumps-immigration-crackdown/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Yappie</a></em> <a href=\"https://theyappie.com/the-hidden-numbers-in-trumps-immigration-crackdown/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">has previously reported</a>, ICE activity involving Asians immigrants has surged at a higher rate than the overall national increase for all immigrants. Immigration doesn’t always stop at the boundaries of immigration status either, as reports of <a href=\"https://theyappie.com/a-new-house-bill-could-enable-wrongfully-detained-u-s-citizens-to-sue-ice/?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">wrongful detentions of citizens</a> show.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>With Miller now serving as chief of staff, it’s unclear whether the Trump administration will actually ease off on deportations.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>AAPI communities already have to navigate the perpetual foreigner stereotype and questions of national loyalty, as evidenced by <a href=\"https://www.scmp.com/tech/big-tech/article/3374435/double-standard-why-jensen-huang-saga-sparking-debate-about-race?utm_campaign=power-shift-4-000-miles-for-care&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_source=newsletters.theyappie.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">recent discourse</a> surrounding Nvidia CEO <strong>Jensen Huang</strong>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator alignwide has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>About <em>The Yappie</em></strong>: <em>The Yappie</em> is an independent, nonprofit newsroom dedicated to tracking Asian American and Pacific Islander power, politics, and influence. Learn more at <a href=\"https://theyappie.com/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">theyappie.com/about</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>","byu":"https://theyappie.com/author/hojunglee/"}